-- title:
--   Two generators modulo kerπ_k for a corner of H¹
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, $k$ a field which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\operatorname{alg}_{\mathcal O\to k}$ surjective, $p \neq 2$ a prime with $\operatorname{char} k = p$, and $M' \geq 1$ with $p \nmid M'$; let $S$ be a finite set of naturals. The module is $H^1(M',\top;\mathcal O) = \operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_{\top}(M')^{\mathrm{add}}, \mathcal O)$, carrying the operators [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) indexed by the generators [`CohCarrier.Gen`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13): $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid M'$ and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M'$ (both given by `heckeTL`), and diamond operators for $d \in (\mathbb Z/M')^\times$; these are assumed to commute pairwise, and $\bar\theta$ is an arbitrary function from the generators to $k$. Let $B$ be the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal O} H^1$ generated by the range of these operators, and let $S'$ be an `IdempotentSplitting` of $B$, i.e. a complete orthogonal family of idempotents $e_i$ ($i < n$) together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ exhausting the maximal ideals of $B$ and satisfying $e_i \in \mathfrak m_j \iff i \neq j$. Fix an index $i_0$ and an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\pi_k$ from the corner ring $e_{i_0} B e_{i_0}$ to $k$ with $\pi_k(e_{i_0} \cdot \operatorname{op}(g) \cdot e_{i_0}) = \bar\theta(g)$ for every generator $g$. Finally let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$ (a two-dimensional $k$-space $V$ with a monoid homomorphism from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to $\operatorname{End}_k V$ factoring through a finite level) which is absolutely irreducible, i.e. irreducible after base change to $\overline{k}$, and assume the Eichler–Shimura type relation: for every prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid M'$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $A$ acting as $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field, $\operatorname{tr} \bar\rho(\sigma) = \bar\theta(T_\ell)$ (no condition $\ell \neq p$ is imposed). The conclusion is that there exist $x, y$ in the corner submodule $e_{i_0} \cdot H^1(M',\top;\mathcal O)$ whose span over the corner ring $e_{i_0} B e_{i_0}$, together with the set of elements $a \cdot m$ with $\pi_k(a) = 0$ and $m$ in that corner submodule, is the whole corner submodule.
--
--   This is the cohomological form, for trivial nebentypus, of the multiplicity-one bound of Wiles, Chapter 2 §1: the corner $e H^1(\Gamma_0(M'),\mathcal O)$ is generated by two elements modulo $\mathfrak m = \ker \pi_k$, equivalently $\dim_k e H^1/\mathfrak m e H^1 \leq 2$ when $\bar\rho$ is absolutely irreducible. It feeds the freeness statements [`CohCarrier.free_sigmaCorner_gammaZero`](thm.html#CohCarrier.free_sigmaCorner_gammaZero) and [`CuspForm.AuxLevel.baseML_free_range_lsmul`](thm.html#CuspForm.AuxLevel.baseML_free_range_lsmul).
